WEBVTT

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.830
"Wanna meet up? By the way,
I heard you on the radio."

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:17.330
"Hey"
"4:44   Mitsuo"

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.330
What the heck is this about? Of all things,
I get a text from my fated lover?!

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.950
Seriously, what's going on?
Is this what it means to become famous?

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:36.000
Hey, really? Well that's embarrassing.
The restaurant is closed on Wednesdays,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.540
so I'm free all day then.
But anyway, how've you been?

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.410
I'm gonna make you cry, just wait.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.000
"I Won't Believe You"

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:20.290
Ahh! Honey!

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:21.620
Honey?

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:23.200
"Episode 9: I Won't Believe You"
I need to borrow your computer!

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.580
"Episode 9: I Won't Believe You"
"Viewing this content is not
supported by your current browser," my ass!

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.700
Miss Minare, it's incredible that
you've been able to live without

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.660
a computer or smartphone all this time.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:34.580
I've been using the computer at the restaurant

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:37.450
and I carelessly used my points
on a new battery for my flip phone,

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:39.290
and I didn't want it to be a waste.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:43.540
I don't care what you think! I've always pursued
small gains and missed out on large ones.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.790
"hunting gun how to purchase"
What in the world are you searching for?!

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:48.750
"hunting gun how to purchase"
So, actually...

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.540
Mr. Mitsuo... You mean that Mr. Mitsuo...?!

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:53.250
That's amazing, Miss Minare.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:55.660
This is what it means to become famous.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:03:01.790
Mizuho, just so you know, this isn't the
romantic love story you're thinking of at all.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:03.200
Let me explain.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.500
This is the guy who wouldn't
pick up my calls and just disappeared

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.000
after milking 500,000 yen out of me.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.250
But you still agreed to meet up with him, right?

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.790
What are you thinking of talking to him about?

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.790
Miss Minare, please keep
things amicable. Please!

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:23.660
Oh, come on Mizuho.
Guns are impossible to obtain, anyway.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:24.660
Right...

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.200
I'm not that crazy.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.700
Well, of course, I'm not that worried...

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:34.410
The training session for obtaining a gun permit
already happened this month.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:37.370
But if I reschedule to meet
with Mitsuo another month,

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:40.700
I think he'd pick up on the unsettling vibes.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:43.000
So I'm going to annihilate him socially.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:48.330
Right now, I've never been so grateful
to be involved with radio.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.330
Just watch, Mitsuo.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:01.120
I bet he'll feel threatened when he
sees me in this aggressive outfit.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.750
Oh, yeah...

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.830
He said he likes light pink lips.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:10.160
I'll wear bright red!

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.500
I heard the news. You're meeting up
with that Mitsuo guy, huh?

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.250
What are you using the recorder for?

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:21.500
Mr. Mato, I'm thinking of switching to
a smartphone before I meet up with Mitsuo.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.620
So what?

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:28.330
I'll bring up that I forgot to take down his
number, so he'll have to tell me verbally.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:31.200
And I'm gonna play that recording on air.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.200
What do you think of this
splendid revenge strategy?

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.500
Uh, well...

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:36.950
"Heeheeheehee..."
"So low..."

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:38.080
"Heeheeheehee..."
"So low..."
"So sinister..."

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:42.700
--Sorry, but I can't let you borrow it
for that kind of purpose.
--Hey!

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.660
What? But why?!

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:48.750
No listener wants to send e-mails
or fax to a radio station

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.620
that might expose their personal
information like it's nothing.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:54.620
There needs to be a journalistic
reason for a radio station

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.500
to expose personal information
without permission.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:02.450
Think about it, Miss Minare. Mr. Mitsuo knows
your address and phone number, too, right?

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:05.620
What if he exposes your information
on the web for revenge?

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.790
You just started your radio program.
It's a crucial period.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.500
Miss Minare, you'd end up
suffering the real damage!

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:13.620
Then what am I supposed to do?!

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:18.870
This means there's no way for
a radio DJ to take revenge at all!

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:20.620
Of course not.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:23.660
A grown adult shouldn't be weeping over this.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:28.290
Minare, as the director who discovered you,
I've got a proposal for you.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:37.080
Oh, there you are! Hey Mina... Mina!

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:41.040
Oh my god... How could
he not change at all?

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.410
--He's always empty-handed,
no matter where he goes.

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:44.250
--Mina!
--He's always empty-handed,
no matter where he goes.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:46.910
It's been a while.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:50.000
He always has that dumb,
carefree smile on his face.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.080
Your lips are so red today.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:58.580
It makes you look older,
so I don't really like it.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:01.450
He's sensitive to a girl's appearance
but brutally honest with his opinions.

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:05.120
So I took the bus here from Maruyama Park...

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:08.580
But it's quite the trek getting here,
don't you think?

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:09.750
--But actually, since the weather was nice,
the wind felt so good.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:13.950
--How could you talk to me like this,
as if nothing happened?!
--But actually, since the weather was nice,
the wind felt so good.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:18.200
Huh? What's wrong?

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.660
No, what's wrong with you?!

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:23.910
Oh, crap. The cable car's arriving soon.

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:24.830
Ah...

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:31.080
Two round trip tickets will be 3,400 yen.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.660
Here.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.200
Wait, hold on...

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:38.790
...1,700 yen for a 14-minute round trip
is pricey, don't you think?

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:41.200
Oh... Yeah, it is...

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:49.290
Please be cautious of the swaying
cable car at the stopping point.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:53.080
That didn't feel right just now...

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.410
But why...?

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:57.250
Oh, whatever...

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.660
Oh... Ah...

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:05.870
Ah... I thought I was sick of this place,
but it feels so good!

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:09.790
Mitsuo's the one who suggested
going on a date to Mt. Moiwa.

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:13.370
If he's fishing for a connection
with Moiwayama Radio...

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:16.620
Where's your radio station, Mina?

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.200
Ah, it's so close.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:20.750
I want to go check it out. Could I get a tour?

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:24.500
Oh, hello. I'm her ex, Mitsuo. Yup, that one.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:29.160
He'd try to steer the conversation like that.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.910
If that really happens...

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:34.750
...I'll push him off and kill him.

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:38.500
Oh, yeah, that's right. I wanna
give you something now, Mina.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:39.910
Huh?

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:43.330
When a friend from junior high
visited the other day,

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:46.080
he brought me this as a gift.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:49.160
Meigetsudo's Hakata Torimon.
You love them, don't you?

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:53.790
Whoa... Thanks... You seriously just
shoved that into your pocket, huh?

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:55.160
But, well...

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:58.370
"The Monde Selection
Gold Label is a weakness..."

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.370
"The Monde Selection
Gold Label is a weakness..."
And also... Here.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.330
What's this?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.910
The money I owe you.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:04.700
What?!

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:07.660
What? Did you forget about
the money you lent me?

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:10.870
Ah... Of course not!

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:14.580
Um, wait... Did you really
come see me to pay me back?

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:16.500
Well, yeah... Of course.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:23.000
But... This doesn't feel like 500,000 yen.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.910
This is only 250,000 yen.

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:31.410
Forgive me, Mina! That's all I've got right now.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.160
I just wanted to demonstrate good faith.

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:35.830
I promise I'll pay you back completely
by the end of the year.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:37.250
December...?!

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:40.040
That means I won't get
any confirmation until then!

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:44.580
I'll be left in limbo between
full repayment and overdue debt!

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:47.750
Schrödinger's debt repayment!

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:50.330
But... But...

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:56.450
There's a part of me that's ready
to forgive him. I'm too easy.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:09:00.580
But the air feels so refreshing
up on the mountain.

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:02.000
No, wait--don't forget!

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.120
For two days after getting his text,

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:06.410
I promised myself I wouldn't
go so far as to kill him,

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:08.750
but at least shatter five or six of his teeth.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:12.290
I used the time between
when Mizuho and I head to work

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:16.370
to practice my high kicks,
train my arms using the turtle tank,

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:18.200
and watch Tony Jaa movies!

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:21.830
The lethality of fluorescent
light is zero, noted.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:24.000
"But it was only two days..."
I won't let those days go to waste!

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.540
Listen...

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:33.450
Yuri told me that she saw you walking with
another girl while you were still dating me.

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.040
Multiple times.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:39.250
I could care less about it now.

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:41.500
But what's your explanation about that?

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:43.830
Oh, boy... What a bust.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:44.750
That girl...

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:46.950
That's right, bring it on!

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:48.870
I put him off guard by saying I could care less.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:50.500
Depending on what he says,

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:54.370
I might kick and break his lower jaw
so hard that it dislocates his hip joint!

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:58.750
That night when I heard you on the radio...

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:01.540
I was almost stabbed and killed by that girl.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.160
Agh... Stabbed and killed?!

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:08.750
You know, it's because you were on the radio
that I'm standing here talking to you today.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:12.160
Ah... This isn't what I wanted...

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:14.120
But...

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:16.250
No freaking way! Tell me more!

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:17.910
Right?!

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:22.080
I wanted to see you so I could
thank you for that, too.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.580
Oh... Um...

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:27.000
Then, should we talk in the lounge downstairs?

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.000
Sure, that works.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.870
Oh, come on. What the heck am I doing?

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:33.790
But I'm getting hungry.

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:35.160
I wanna eat curry!

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:36.450
Aw...

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:41.000
No! Wait, hold on! That "aw" was
because of my intercostal neuralgia!

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.910
Oh... Then... Should we go into that restaurant?

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.250
Let's head back. There's a shop
I want to check out.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.750
Why did we climb up here in the first place?

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:52.160
"Moiwayama Limited Edition!! Morisu Merch"
To celebrate our reunion,
I wanted to buy you something, Mina.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:53.700
You love Morisu, don't you?

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:59.000
I was collecting Morisu merch
when I first moved to Sapporo.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:02.950
Plus, I probably have everything
besides the boxers.

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:06.370
Looks like a knock-off of Kumamon, as always.

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:10.290
Morisu has been around longer.
I've told you so many times.

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:14.450
So, going back to this subject...

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:19.040
That means you were cheating on me, then.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:20.750
I could care less about it now.

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:24.200
I actually wanted to go to
the restaurant you work at, Mina.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.910
They're closed on Wednesdays
and that's why I'm here.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.620
Oh...

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:32.290
But I don't think it was cheating...

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:35.870
She sat next to me when I
went out drinking with a friend.

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:38.870
I guess she got attached to me
as we hit it off talking.

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:42.830
We would go have tea, talk on the phone,
and let each other borrow books.

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:46.700
Somewhere along there, she started
thinking that she was my girlfriend.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.910
Let me ask you, point blank.

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.540
Did you do it with her or not?!

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:54.410
Of course not! I was still with you, Mina.

00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:59.370
That night, she swung a bat at the back of my
head in front of the apartment and I passed out.

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:00.450
Seriously?

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:04.910
When I came to, I was on the dining room floor
in my room with my hands and legs tied up.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:10.000
When she put the knife on my face,
that's when we heard your voice from the phone.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:13.620
I guess she related to a lot
of the things you were saying,

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:18.040
so she screamed out the front door
and got hit by a car.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:19.200
She's in the hospital right now.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.500
How could you smile telling that story?

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:24.910
If she related to a lot of
the things from that broadcast,

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:28.200
she must've lent Mitsuo money, too.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:30.250
Most likely the same exact amount.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:33.250
She freaked out because I was telling her story.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:39.000
That's because he used the same
exact lie he told me to deceive her.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:43.330
Moreover, if she attacked him
in front of his apartment...

00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:47.160
That means she'd been to his place!
They totally did it.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.330
Mitsuo... You--

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:52.830
There aren't any girls out there
better than you, Mina.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:53.830
Huh?

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:55.580
Oh, sorry. What was that?

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.870
Uh... I...

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:03.370
I'm going to order more coffee. How about you?

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:05.750
Oh, yeah. I want some, too.

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:08.200
"Densha-Dori's Soup Curry Coffee House
Established 1957"

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:11.790
It's good to eat soup curry
that's not from work sometimes.

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:15.200
I didn't expect you to treat me, either.

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.700
I told you today was a celebration.

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.040
Oh, yeah...

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:22.120
I know why I felt uncomfortable
at the ticket office.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.120
"Step 1: Buy 2 tickets"

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:24.120
"Step 2: Give him a ticket"

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:25.410
"Step 3: He pays me back"

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:29.500
"Step 3: He pays me back"
Step 3... That was something
I've rarely experienced before.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:36.790
And that was the first time he paid
me back without me reminding him.

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:41.950
When people experience being on the verge
of death, they completely transform...

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.700
Do you wanna come over to my place?

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:50.790
Sure, I guess.

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:53.950
What the heck am I doing?

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:58.870
We're home! Oh, I'm spent.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:00.910
Mina, could you make us some coffee?

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:03.200
There's a roll cake in the fridge.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:06.910
Okay, fine. I know your place inside out.

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.250
Huh?

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:21.160
We ended up hanging out all day!

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:22.540
After that...

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:25.870
We went day-drinking at Autumn Fest,

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:28.330
watched a movie at Sapporo Factory,

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:30.290
went bowling at Norbesa,

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:32.660
and even rode their Ferris wheel!

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:36.580
Honestly, it was actually
a little, no... really fun.

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:39.620
Because it's been a while
since I've been on a date!

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:41.540
What is going on with me?

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:46.120
Is this the same woman who was saying until
yesterday that she'd shoot him to death?

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:50.330
It's not too late to poison his coffee...

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:52.870
Ah, you take milk and no sugar, right?

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:54.330
Yup. Thanks.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.500
How could there be no poison in this house?!

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:58.080
Why are you pissed off?

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:00.040
Here.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:02.790
I got a little hungry, so I cut
two slices for each of us.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.080
Yay.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:07.410
I realized after making the coffee, but don't
you think we should've had Japanese tea instead?

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:10.290
We drank coffee at the restaurant
and at the movie theater.

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:12.950
It's fine. Cake goes best with coffee.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:15.200
You're regretting how you asked me out of habit

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:19.540
to make you coffee as soon
as you got home, right?

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:20.870
I am not!

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:22.330
You were like this all day.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:25.000
Beer goes best with meat!

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:25.580
"Dude, we just had curry..."
Beer goes best with meat!

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:28.120
"Dude, we just had curry..."
You're not eating it at all.

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:31.450
That was an all-Japanese cast.
What do you think of that?

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:35.370
It's fine. I wanted to watch it
because I'm a fan of the book.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:38.080
He's the type to be controlled
by his preferences.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:42.200
Well, that's part of his charm, I guess.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:44.950
Mitsuo, let's eat the chicken we just bought.

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:46.200
And we'll drink.

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:48.040
Ah, good idea.

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:50.370
There's actually beer in the fridge.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:53.290
Yup, I saw that earlier.

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:55.080
All right, cheers! What a day.

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:56.200
What a day.

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:58.080
Celebrating our reunion and reconciliation.

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:00.290
What? Not so fast, dude.

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:03.660
My heart will be shut tight until
you pay me back the full amount.

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:05.790
Oh, yeah. That's right.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:08.540
You're a stubborn one, Mina.

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:13.870
And just because you pay me back doesn't
mean you can earn my trust back that easily.

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:16.080
You lied to me, you know?

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:17.250
Sorry.

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:20.830
I became a co-signer for my friend's debt.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.200
But I can't get in contact with him right now.

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:26.950
I just didn't want to make you worry, Mina.

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:30.620
You could've told me that in the first place!
Isn't that what your girlfriend is there for?

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:34.830
You didn't want to make me worry, but you
were okay borrowing money from me?

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:37.500
Sorry! But I was planning on paying you back.

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:41.200
Jeez...

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:48.790
--Hey!
--Ah... I missed your thighs, Mina.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:51.200
--Ah... I missed your thighs, Mina.

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.700
I'm so glad you came back.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:58.910
--Let me clean your ears.
--What?

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:03.250
Don't play dumb. If you lie there,
that's what's gonna happen.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.080
Ah, you're right.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:07.580
And... I didn't come back yet.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:09.790
You better not have thrown away Onikirimaru.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:11.620
"*Onikirimaru -- Minare's ear pick
that has been sharpened like a sword."
You better not have thrown away Onikirimaru.

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:13.120
"*Onikirimaru -- Minare's ear pick
that has been sharpened like a sword."
Oh, yeah.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:15.790
Found him.

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:19.620
It's been a while since
I cleaned it, so surely...

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:21.870
Yes! It's the gold rush!

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:23.620
You seem happy.

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:26.290
I read on the internet that it's not good
to clean your ears too much.

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:31.410
Whatever. I'm cleaning your ears
for my own sake and pleasure.

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:33.830
But...

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:39.000
I'll cut you a break today... Okay, other ear.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:43.950
Before I do that... I want you
to put chicken in my mouth.

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:49.700
Hey! You do realize I was thinking of ways
to kill you until only yesterday?

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:51.870
But here, I'll feed you.

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:52.870
Yum.

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:56.750
It's so good!

00:17:56.750 --> 00:17:58.370
What a baby...

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:04.660
I prefer light-colored lips... Just saying.

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:09.750
Dammit, fine then...

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:14.120
This is the horror of the man-child.

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:18.910
He makes the woman think she's
taking the lead. But actually...

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:21.910
The woman becomes subservient to him.

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:25.370
Huh?

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:28.750
What's up?

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:31.000
Huh? Nothing...

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:36.870
The coffee-flavored kiss.

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:38.870
You love them, don't you?

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:40.000
Huh?

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:45.120
Ah... Huh...?

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:50.830
So tell me... How did you really
spend my 500,000 yen?

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:53.410
What? I told you I became a co-signer...

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.040
At the Sapporo race tracks...

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:03.700
How did you manage to find the 250,000 yen?

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:06.660
Well... I guess this was two months ago...

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:08.750
Someone related to an oil company executive

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:12.790
moved in on the floor above me,
and I was being nice to them.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:16.540
I helped them move their furniture
and suggested good restaurants.

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:18.700
I was hoping to get something in return.

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:23.700
And alas, they secretly gave me a share
of their unlisted stock last week.

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:24.500
So that's how.

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:26.410
That's questionable money!

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:29.620
How else would I get a lump sum of cash?

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:31.450
I work part-time cleaning four days a week.

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:36.330
Listen! It's about time you think
about modest happiness.

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:39.250
Don't expect to get rich quick like that.

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:41.370
It's okay if you don't make that much money.

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:46.450
You can eat out less and learn how to
cook cheap and delicious meals.

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:48.290
I can teach you how to do that!

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:51.450
In any case, if you keep spending
everything you make,

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:54.410
and relying on other people's
money, you're gonna--

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:56.000
It's gonna be fine.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.500
I have no interest in cooking at all.

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:03.870
Why should I cook when there're lots
of cheap and delicious restaurants?

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:05.250
Yeah...

00:20:05.250 --> 00:20:07.040
Thought so...

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:09.540
I just wanted to confirm, just in case.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:16.580
So tell me...

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:20.870
Do you have any idea what this is?

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:22.120
O-Oh...

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:26.830
This is a free magazine that has
a month's worth of recipes.

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:29.660
You can find this at any co-op in Hokkaido.

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:33.160
I'm sure you threw this away since
you have no interest in these things.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:39.790
But if this is here, it must mean someone who's
interested in cooking was here in this room.

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:41.410
Somebody besides me...

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:43.250
O-Oh...

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:45.080
See? Look at this.

00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:47.410
It's a dried-up bell pepper seed.

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:50.910
What's a recipe that uses bell peppers in here?

00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:52.620
Chinese stir-fry, perhaps?

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:54.910
That's your favorite dish, isn't it?

00:20:54.910 --> 00:20:58.660
A person who wants to make that for you...

00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:02.750
...is someone who wants you
so badly. Isn't that right?

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:07.410
If you act like you're destitute for money
in front of a person like that...

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:10.370
I'm sure they'd lend it to you.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:13.160
Just like I did.

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:16.790
You almost got yourself killed because
she found out you were lying.

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:17.950
Isn't that right?

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:26.450
Unlisted stock, my ass. You think you're
so clever, huh? Well I'd say you're a genius!

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:28.330
You're a woman's enemy.

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:37.370
He's stubborn and vain... But really nice.

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:39.790
He always has a smile on his face.

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:42.910
But...

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:46.580
When he lies to you with that smile...
It's unbearable.

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:54.120
Mitsuo, you can keep the remaining
250,000 yen as a settlement.

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:58.750
There's no way I'm gonna make you
betray another woman just to pay me back.

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:30.120
"Next Episode"

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:30.700
"Next Episode"
Kakoton, Kakoen, there's a job for you.

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:32.330
"Preview"
Kakoton, Kakoen, there's a job for you.

00:23:32.330 --> 00:23:34.250
"Preview"
The legendary duo has been summoned!

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:35.080
"Preview"
Legendary?

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:36.290
"Preview"
Nobody knows their real name.

00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:37.750
"Preview"
What kind of company is this?

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:40.870
Minare, bury Mitsuo for the next broadcast.

00:23:40.870 --> 00:23:43.540
Bury him... What do you mean?

00:23:43.540 --> 00:23:45.950
This is the burial of Mitsuo... and you.

00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:47.080
So what do you mean by that?!

00:23:47.080 --> 00:23:49.450
It's the audio drama,
"Tale of the Sea of Trees."

00:23:49.450 --> 00:23:52.660
Minare, die and reincarnate with Mitsuo.

00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:58.950
Next on <i>Wave, Listen to Me!</i>:
"I Have to Do This."

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:01.910
"Illustrated by Hiroaki Samura"
"See you next time!"
